"[2601.15621v1] Qwen3-TTS Technical Report (https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.15621v1)\nciteturn27736view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.15621v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 164\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Sound\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 22 Jan 2026]\nL9: # Title:Qwen3-TTS Technical Report\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Hangrui Hu , cite6†Xinfa Zhu , cite7†Ting He , cite8†Dake Guo , cite9†Bin Zhang , cite10†Xiong Wang , cite11†Zhifang Guo , cite12†Ziyue Jiang , cite13†Hongkun Hao , cite11†Zishan Guo , cite14†Xinyu Zhang , cite15†Pei Zhang , cite16†Baosong Yang , cite17†Jin Xu , cite18†Jingren Zhou , cite19†Junyang Lin L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Qwen3-TTS Technical Report, by Hangrui Hu and 15 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite20†View PDF cite21†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:In this report, we present the Qwen3-TTS series, a family of advanced multilingual, controllable, robust, and streaming text-to-speech models. Qwen3-TTS supports state-of-the-art 3-second voice cloning and description-based control, allowing both the creation of entirely novel voices and fine-grained manipulation over the output speech.\nL17: Trained on over 5 million hours of speech data spanning 10 languages, Qwen3-TTS adopts a dual-track LM architecture for real-time synthesis, coupled with two speech tokenizers: 1) Qwen-TTS-Tokenizer-25Hz is a single-codebook codec emphasizing semantic content, which offers seamlessly integration with Qwen-Audio and enables streaming waveform reconstruction via a block-wise DiT.\nL18: 2) Qwen-TTS-Tokenizer-12Hz achieves extreme bitrate reduction and ultra-low-latency streaming, enabling immediate first-packet emission ($97\\,\\mathrm{ms}$) through its 12.5 Hz, 16-layer multi-codebook design and a lightweight causal ConvNet. Extensive experiments indicate state-of-the-art performance across diverse objective and subjective benchmark (e.g., TTS multilingual test set, InstructTTSEval, and our long speech test set).\nL19: To facilitate community research and development, we release both tokenizers and models under the Apache 2.0 license.\nL20: Comments:  | cite22†this https URL†github.com L21: Subjects:  | Sound (cs.SD); Computation and Language (cs.CL); Audio and Speech Processing (eess.AS)\nL22: Cite as:  | cite23†arXiv:2601.15621 [cs.SD]\nL23:    | (or cite24†arXiv:2601.15621v1 [cs.SD] for this version)\nL24:    | cite25†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2601.15621†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Jin Xu [cite26†view email ]\nL28: [v1] Thu, 22 Jan 2026 03:51:43 UTC (7,505 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled Qwen3-TTS Technical Report, by Hangrui Hu and 15 other authors\nL35: \nL36:   * cite20†View PDF L37:   * cite21†HTML (experimental) L38:   * cite27†TeX Source L39: \nL40: cite28†view license†creativecommons.org L41: \nL42: ### Current browse context:\nL43: \nL44: cs.SD\nL45: \nL46: cite29†< prev |   cite30†next > L47: \nL48: cite31†new | cite32†recent | cite33†2026-01 L49: \nL50: Change to browse by:\nL51: \nL52: cite34†cs L53: cite35†cs.CL L54: cite36†eess L55: cite37†eess.AS L56: ### References & Citations\nL57: \nL58:   * cite38†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L59:   * cite39†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L60:   * cite40†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L61: \nL62: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL63: \nL64: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL65: \nL66: [Button: ×]\nL67: \nL68: loading...\nL69: \nL70: Data provided by:\nL71